 "result": "Full suite passes.\n\n**Root cause**: `Sentinel` enum members use `object()` as their values. `enum.Enum.__reduce_ex__` pickles by reconstructing `Sentinel(self._value_)`, but a fresh `object()` deserializes as a *new, unequal* instance, so unpickling raised `ValueError: <object object at ...> is not a valid Sentinel`. `copy`/`deepcopy` already worked correctly since `Enum.__copy__`/`__deepcopy__` just return `self`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/click/_utils.py`): overrode `Sentinel.__reduce_ex__` to reconstruct by name (`getattr(self.__class__, self._name_)`) instead of by value, so pickling correctly returns the same singleton.\n\nAdded a parametrized test in `tests/test_utils/test_sentinel.py` covering `copy`, `deepcopy`, and `pickle` (all protocols) for both `UNSET` and `FLAG_NEEDS_VALUE`. Full test suite (1916 passed) still green.",
